## Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

### Implementation Summary

**Framework Detected:** React with Vite (identified from package.json and vite.config.js)

**Documentation Source:** Latest installation instructions fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### Changes Made

1. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
   - Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
   - Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependencies

2. **Analytics Integration**
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react"`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component to the main App component in `src/App.jsx`
   - Positioned the Analytics component at the root level of the app to track all page views

### Files Modified

- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package resolution
- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added following the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects:
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/react` as specified in the docs
- Placed inside the main App div to ensure it's rendered on all pages
- No additional configuration needed - the component will automatically track page views

### Verification Steps Completed

✓ Package installed successfully via npm
✓ Build completed without errors (vite build)
✓ No new linting errors introduced in App.jsx
✓ All changes properly staged for commit

### Next Steps

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard (Analytics tab)
2. Verify the `/_vercel/insights/*` routes are accessible
3. Monitor the Analytics dashboard for incoming data after user visits

### Notes

- The project uses npm as the package manager
- Build artifacts were excluded from staging (dist/ folder)
